<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n110994" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φίλημ-α</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῐ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>, τό, 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φίλᾱμα</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Mosch.
			1.5
		</span></i>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>kiss,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				135
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				1.3.12
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. δοῦναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IA</u>
					679
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				1238
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. παρὰ γένυν τιθέντα σόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					1154
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πατρὶ . . διὰ φιλημάτων ἰών</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Andr.</u>
					416
				</span></i>
			; of kisses as prizes in a game, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παίζωμεν περὶ φιλημάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.Com.
					46
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				537
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eub.
				3.4
			</span></i>; as a symbol of Christian love, <i><span class="en">
				<u>1 Ep.Cor.</u>
				16.20
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> pl.,
				<i>cosmetics,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ach.Tat.
				2.38
			</span></i> (fort. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φαρμάκων</span>).</div>
